  "details": "I'm posting this from the perspective of a group owner/moderators where it would apply the most, but this could theoretically be useful for other instance types, too.\n\nFor popular worlds that have a cap of 80 or otherwise high cap, it would be useful for group instance hosters to be able to set their own cap that's lower than the world author's. This would allow groups that don't have a large moderation team or who prefer a calmer environment for their instances to moderate worlds they otherwise wouldn't host at.\n\nA specific example of a group instance would be Naku's music events. In some rare cases, we've reached out to a world creator directly to request a temporarily lower cap. But, we skip out on a fair amount of beautiful worlds that otherwise would be hosted at because the mod team just isn't big enough to handle the level of traffic through the world.\n\nI would imagine this to be a setting exposed to those with instance/moderation rights in groups during the instance creation dialog. World owners would be able to opt out if they felt that a lower instance cap could detract from the world experience.",
